        "comments": "The assembly dcClaSibi1.hap1.1 is based on 65x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Multiple haplotypic inversions were observed on chromosome 2 (90-125 Mbp), chromosome 3 168.7-175.3 Mbp), chromosome 4 (52-113.4 Mbp & 132.1-155.7 Mbp), chromosome 5 (91.7-132.3 Mbp) and chromosome 6 (31.7-42.8 Mbp & 148.3-168.4 Mbp).",
